	"narrative": {
		"northStar": "The Persistent Navigation Spine",
		"overview": "Accent's shipped interface is an internal work tool: dense, flat, and organized around one fixed navigation spine. The current shell is the shadcn sidebar at the left — a white 16rem panel that collapses to a 3rem icon rail without losing state — paired with a separate, still-shipping legacy top navbar that carries broad section links and the Accent logo. Neither layer replaces the other in the build; new screens inherit both.\n\nThe palette is white plus five purple steps: deep brand purple for text, icons, active fills and primary buttons; lavender for selection and separators; a lighter purple for focus. Surfaces sit flat, corners use an 0.5rem base radius, and the icon language is Lucide at a single 16px stroke size inside the sidebar (the older navbar uses outline Heroicons at 20px). Page content uses the same purple on cards and headers, but this document records only rules that are actually reused across the shell.",
		"keyCharacteristics": [
			"White sidebar shell with deep-purple text and icons; no dark mode (backgrounds are forced white).",
			"Two widths only: 16rem expanded, 3rem collapsed icon rail (18rem mobile sheet).",
			"Lavender selection fill with matching purple foreground; lilac 1px separators.",
			"Flat surfaces; the only shell shadow is on the fixed top navbar.",
			"Poppins body face loaded in the root layout; Geist Mono for code and metrics.",
			"Lucide icons in the sidebar; outline Heroicons in the legacy navbar."
